From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:02:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] milkflint tests: check what mutation testing showed unchecked

Mutation testing put small bugs into the driver; each of these survived every
test. Now they're caught:
- mt7915 tx-free events: tx stays blocked while freeing leaves the token
  pool at its threshold (both event formats).
- mt7915 restart: the MT7986 has no second host interface, so its INT1
  registers are left alone; the interrupt mask comes back.
- mt7915 SER reset: the tx worker is running again and the tx NAPI was
  kicked afterwards.
- Firmware commands: eBF is off for a VHT station that isn't a beamformee;
  the rate control TLV carries the station's bandwidth in phy.bw too; MCU
  frames go out with no DMA descriptor info; tx power takes the best chain
  even when it's the first; band 1 turns on its noise floor measurement
  when it starts.
- mt76 core: every tx queue counts as pending, not just BE; the driver's
  set_channel runs under the device mutex; an asleep station repeating
  its PM bit, or one without PS tracking, changes nothing; removing a
  station ends the BA sessions of TID 0 and 15 too and leaves its queue
  locks free; a 6 GHz band gets every OFDM rate; a message payload longer
  than its length still gets the bus tailroom.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
